  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (cells 18–20, exact at point 1, finite twist)\n\n- **Single labels.** The only SoV covector that acts on site 2 only is the vacuum $100|100$. By contrast, site 1 has 4 single labels ($100,111,200,211$ on site 1, with site 2 in $100$).\n- **Combinations.** $\\sum_xc_x\\langle x|=\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}\\otimes w|$ is again an **8-dimensional** space, and its site-2 covectors $w\\,g_0^{-1}$ have **rank 8** (cell 20), so every site-2 weight is reached. But it uses **35 of the 64 labels** (site 1 uses 12). Its reduced-row-echelon basis has supports of sizes $1,2,3,5,6,6,10,12$.\n- **Minimal supports up to size 5** span only **4 of the 8** dimensions:\n\n| minimal combination | coefficients | site-2 weights of $w\\,g_0^{-1}$ |\n|---|---|---|\n| $100\\|100$ | 1 | $(2,1,0)$ |\n| $100\\|200,\\ 200\\|100$ | $-10/19,\\ 1$ | $(2,1,0),(1,2,0)$ |\n| $100\\|110,\\ 100\\|200,\\ 110\\|100$ | $-10/19,\\ -9/19,\\ 1$ | $(2,1,0),(2,0,1)$ |\n| $100\\|111,\\ 111\\|100,\\ 200\\|110,\\ 200\\|200,\\ 210\\|100$ | $200/2679,\\ -5/24,\\ -20/47,\\ -9/14,\\ 1$ | (not tabulated) |\n\n  (There is one more size-3 support, $\\{100|110, 110|100, 200|100\\}$, but it depends on the rows above.)\n- **Asymmetry.** $\\langle x_{g_1|g_2}|=\\langle\\mathrm{vacL}^{\\otimes2}|O_{g_1}(\\theta_1)O_{g_2}(\\theta_2)$ applies the site-1 operators first, so a site-2 localizing combination has to cancel site-1 excitations, and that mixes many labels. The pairs still trade a site-2 label for the mirrored site-1 label ($100|200\\leftrightarrow200|100$). Coefficients seen so far are $-10/19=\\theta_{12}-h$ and $-9/19=-\\theta_{12}$ (with $\\theta_{12}=9/19$, $h=1$), compared with $-1/\\theta_{12}$ on site 1. These identifications come from one point only.\n- Not done: supports of size ≥ 6 (1.6M subsets).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
